{"id":"debug-trl-grpo","benchmark":"skillsbench","instruction":"# debug-trl-grpo\n\nI am training a countdown math task using TRL for my model with GRPO, but the new model shows no improvement. \nThe source code is at /app/trl. Check if there is any bug and fix them. \n\nDO NOT modify the training script (`/app/train_grpo.py`) or reward function (`/app/reward_fn.py`)","supplemental":[],"items":[{"item_id":"B1-logprob","requirement":"The log-probability computation in TRL (selective_log_softmax) must produce values numerically equivalent to standard log_softmax-then-gather, must always be non-positive, and must yield a log probability close to 0 for the token with the highest logit.","source_quote":"Check if there is any bug and fix them.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_selective_log_softmax_correctness; test_outputs.py::test_log_probs_nonpositive; test_outputs.py::test_log_probs_highest_token","verification":"A grader can verify this by running the three selective_log_softmax tests: comparing its output against F.log_softmax(...).gather(...) within 1e-5 tolerance on random float32 logits, confirming all outputs are <= 0, and confirming the log-prob of a dominant (highest-logit) token lies strictly between -1.0 and 0.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"B1-logprob","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"B2-advantage-eps","requirement":"The epsilon added to the standard deviation when normalizing GRPO advantages (advantages = advantages / (std_grouped_rewards + eps)) in grpo_trainer.py must be a small numerical-stability constant (well under 1.0), so advantages do not vanish when group rewards vary.","source_quote":"Check if there is any bug and fix them.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_advantage_epsilon_reasonable; test_outputs.py::test_advantages_not_vanishing","verification":"A grader can verify this by reading the advantage-scaling line in trl/trainer/grpo_trainer.py, extracting the epsilon constant and confirming it is under 1.0, then recomputing advantages for a varied-reward group ([1.0, 0.0, 0.5, 0.0]) using that epsilon and confirming the resulting max absolute advantage exceeds 0.1.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"B2-advantage-eps","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"B3-decode-strip","requirement":"decode_and_strip_padding in trl/trainer/utils.py must decode completions so that plain text without <think> tags passes through unchanged, text with a closed <think>...</think> block has that block stripped while content after it is kept, and text with an unclosed <think> tag (no matching </think>) decodes to an empty string.","source_quote":"Check if there is any bug and fix them.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_decode_preserves_plain_completions; test_outputs.py::test_decode_extracts_after_think; test_outputs.py::test_decode_handles_incomplete_think","verification":"A grader can verify this by tokenizing three sample completions (plain text, text with a closed think block, text with an unclosed think tag) using the DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B tokenizer, running each through decode_and_strip_padding, and checking that the plain case retains its <answer> tag, the closed-think case retains <answer> but drops the <think> block, and the unclosed-think case returns an empty string.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"B3-decode-strip","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"B3-e2e-reward","requirement":"After decode_and_strip_padding processes a model completion (with or without a <think> block), feeding the decoded text into the unmodified countdown_reward function must yield the correct nonzero reward (1.0) for completions that correctly reach the target using the given numbers.","source_quote":"Check if there is any bug and fix them.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_reward_nonzero_after_decode","verification":"A grader can verify this by decoding three tokenized sample completions via decode_and_strip_padding and passing them into reward_fn.countdown_reward with matching prompt/target/nums arguments, confirming each returns the expected reward of 1.0.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"B3-e2e-reward","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"no-modify-scripts","requirement":"The training script /app/train_grpo.py and the reward function /app/reward_fn.py must remain unmodified while fixing bugs elsewhere in the TRL source.","source_quote":"DO NOT modify the training script (`/app/train_grpo.py`) or reward function (`/app/reward_fn.py`)","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_train_script_not_modified; test_outputs.py::test_reward_fn_not_modified","verification":"A grader can verify this by computing the SHA-256 hash of /app/train_grpo.py and /app/reward_fn.py and confirming they match the original pre-task hashes.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"no-modify-scripts","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"trl-source-intact","requirement":"The TRL source code at /app/trl (including trainer/utils.py and trainer/grpo_trainer.py) must remain present as real, loadable Python source that has been fixed in place, rather than deleted or replaced.","source_quote":"The source code is at /app/trl.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_trl_source_exists","verification":"A grader can verify this by importing trl.trainer.utils and confirming both its __file__ path and the trl/trainer/grpo_trainer.py path exist on disk.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"trl-source-intact","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}}],"runs":[{"id":"codex-with-skills__azure-foundry-openai-gpt-5.2-codex-src-paper-v1-refill-20260615-runner05-xhigh||debug-trl-grpo","label":"codex-with-skills · azure-foundry-openai-gp